.TH RELAYFORGE-SERVICE 8 "" "RelayForge" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
relayforge-service \- native RelayForge Wi-Fi sharing service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/lib/relayforge/relayforge-service --native-networkmanager
.br
.B /usr/lib/relayforge/relayforge-service --native-create-ap --legacy-root ROOT
.br
.B /usr/lib/relayforge/relayforge-service --init-config PATH
.RB [ --wifi-interface NAME ]
.RB [ --ssid NAME ]
.RB [ --backend networkmanager|create_ap ]
.br
.B /usr/lib/relayforge/relayforge-service --migrate-config PATH
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --detect-interface | --wifi-interface NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Normally started by the selected packaged systemd unit. The service exposes the
existing Wi-Fi Hotspot D-Bus interface with Polkit authorization. Installing a
package does not initialize credentials, start the service or activate sharing.
.SH INITIALIZATION
Use an absolute protected path and a real Wi-Fi interface. Initialization creates
fresh random credentials and refuses to overwrite an existing configuration.
Select the backend explicitly. Refer to the packaged README for the service unit
and setup sequence appropriate to the package.
.SH MIGRATION
Migration operates on an administrator-owned mode-0600 offline copy. Writes to
the live /etc/wifi-hotspot.conf are refused. Dry-run reports planned changes
without writing. Only the exact retained factory template receives a new random
password; customized credentials and settings are preserved. Interface repair
requires explicit opt-in and observed adapter evidence. Migration does not
activate sharing or modify the network.
.SH EXPERIMENTAL BAND SWITCHING
Appending --allow-band-switch to a native service command enables the explicit,
authorized SwitchBandAndReconnect request while sharing is stopped. Packaged
units omit this flag. Ordinary Start always preserves the existing upstream.
The controller targets a fresh same-network scanned AP using the existing
profile, without editing settings or requesting secrets. Profiles pinned to a
band, BSSID or channel are refused. Stop/sleep request guarded restoration;
ambiguous activation or external changes retain a private recovery journal and
block further startup. Inspect the upstream before resolving retained evidence.
Only private-bus simulation has been validated; use requires a controlled session.
See /usr/share/doc/relayforge/docs/native-feature-policy.md for ownership and
recovery limits.
.SH EXPERIMENTAL EXISTING BRIDGE
Appending --allow-existing-bridge to a native create_ap service command permits
SHARE_METHOD=bridge only when INTERNET_IFACE is an existing active Linux bridge
and NO_VIRT=0. Packaged units omit this flag. The service adds only a newly owned
virtual AP child. It does not create/delete the bridge, move upstream addresses
or routes, alter bridge policy, or acquire DHCP, DNS, NAT or forwarding resources.
Ownership journals bind the boot/namespace, bridge, parent radio and child.
Changed identities, foreign membership or ambiguous cleanup retain evidence.
The bridge must already have an administrator-assigned MAC; automatic bridge MAC
selection is refused rather than reconfigured. Hardware traffic and
driver validation require a dedicated bench; only simulated interfaces have been
tested. Existing bridge integration is experimental.
.SH LIMITS
Automatic upstream band switching and new bridge/upstream migration are unavailable. Radio and
configuration blockers are exposed through GetCapabilities and desktop failure
messages. Offline test results do not certify drivers or live network behavior.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/wifi-hotspot.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wifi-hotspot-settings (1)
